# Filing statuses

`FilingStatus` is `"single" | "mfj" | "hoh"`. It is stored on the household,
not inferred from people count. MFJ holds two people; single and HOH hold one
(`maxPeople`). Dependents are not modeled: HOH is a user assertion.

## Resolution layer

Never index a tax table with `table[filingStatus]` directly. Use `forFiling`
from `src/lib/config/filingStatus.ts`.

- Federal tables require an explicit `hoh` key (real IRS numbers).
- Medicare IRMAA has no HOH schedule: `tiers` is a `FilingTable` and HOH
  aliases to `single`.
- State tables are **partial by design**. `single` and `mfj` are required;
  `hoh` is optional. Today CA, NY, and NJ carry distinct HOH brackets /
  deductions. Every other state aliases to `single`.

`TABLE_FALLBACK` is `hoh → single`. If neither the status nor its base key
exists, `forFiling` throws and names the dataset.

## UI

Filing-status options come from `FILING_STATUS_ORDER` / `FILING_STATUS_LABELS`,
not hardcoded literals. HOH shows a help note: the status is static for the
whole projection (it often ends mid-horizon in real life), and most states
approximate HOH as single.

`migrateHousehold` heals an unrecognized `filingStatus` to `"single"` and
leaves a stored `"hoh"` alone. Older clients cannot read `hoh` plans.
